      "name" : "Chicken Shawarma",
      "unlockDate" : 759193200,
      "id" : "7D04D238-F1F7-4FDC-99C3-536841BC292C",
      "hasBeenOpened" : false
    },
    {
      "hasBeenOpened" : false,
      "steps" : "Instructions\n1. Prepare the Vegetables:\n - Heat a teaspoon of sesame oil in a skillet. Sauté each vegetable (carrots, zucchini, and mushrooms) separately for 2-3 minutes until softened. Season lightly with salt. Set aside.\n2. Cook the Meat (if using):\n- In a bowl, mix the ground meat with garlic, soy sauce, sesame oil, sugar, and black pepper.\n- Heat a skillet and cook the meat mixture over medium heat until browned. Set aside.\n3. Prepare the Gochujang Sauce:\n- In a small bowl, combine gochujang, sesame oil, sugar, rice vinegar, sesame seeds, and garlic. Mix until smooth. Adjust sweetness or spice level to taste.\n4. Assemble the Bowl:\n- Place a generous serving of rice in a bowl. Arrange the sautéed vegetables, cooked meat, spinach, bean sprouts, and kimchi (if using) around the edges.\n- Place a fried egg on top of the rice.\n5. Garnish and Serve:\n- Drizzle the gochujang sauce over the bowl. Sprinkle with toasted sesame seeds and green onions.\n6. Mix and Enjoy:\n- Before eating, mix everything thoroughly in the bowl to combine flavors and textures.\n\n\nEnjoy your homemade Bibimbap! 🥢",
      "name" : "Bibimbap",
      "ingredients" : "For the Bowl:\n\t•\t2 cups cooked white rice (short-grain preferred)\n\t•\t1 carrot, julienned\n\t•\t1 zucchini, julienned\n\t•\t1 cup spinach (blanched and squeezed)\n\t•\t1 cup bean sprouts (blanched and drained)\n\t•\t4-6 shiitake mushrooms, sliced\n\t•\t1 cup kimchi (optional)\n\t•\t4 eggs (fried or sunny-side-up)\n\t•\t1 teaspoon sesame oil (for cooking vegetables)\n\nFor the Meat (optional):\n\t•\t200g (7 oz) ground beef, chicken, or pork\n\t•\t2 garlic cloves, minced\n\t•\t2 tablespoons soy sauce\n\t•\t1 tablespoon sesame oil\n\t•\t1 tablespoon sugar\n\t•\t1\/4 teaspoon black pepper\n\nFor Gochujang Sauce:\n\t•\t3 tablespoons gochujang (Korean red chili paste)\n\t•\t1 tablespoon sesame oil\n\t•\t1 tablespoon sugar\n\t•\t1 teaspoon rice vinegar (optional)\n\t•\t1 teaspoon toasted sesame seeds\n\t•\t1 teaspoon minced garlic\n\nGarnish:\n\t•\tToasted sesame seeds\n\t•\tSliced green onions",
      "unlockDate" : 759711600,
