    },
    {
      "steps" : "1. Prepare the Meat and Broth:\n- Place the meat in a large pot. Add enough water to cover it completely.\n- Add the halved onion, bay leaves, black peppercorns, and salt. Bring to a boil, then reduce the heat and simmer for 2-3 hours, or until the meat is tender and falls off the bone.\n- Skim off any foam or impurities that rise to the surface during cooking.\n- Once cooked, remove the meat and set it aside. Strain the broth and keep it warm for later use.\n\n2. Make the Noodles:\n- In a mixing bowl, combine the flour and salt. Add the egg and mix, gradually adding water until a firm dough forms.\n- Knead the dough for 5-7 minutes until smooth. Cover and let it rest for 20 minutes.\n- Roll the dough out thinly (about 1-2 mm thick) and cut into squares or diamond shapes (about 3-4 inches wide). Set aside.\n\n3. Cook the Noodles:\n- Bring a portion of the reserved broth to a boil in a separate pot.\n- Add the noodles to the boiling broth and cook for 2-3 minutes, or until tender. Remove with a slotted spoon and keep warm.\n\n4. Prepare the Onion Sauce:\n- In a skillet, melt the butter or lamb fat over medium heat.\n- Add the sliced onions and sauté until soft and translucent, about 5-7 minutes.\n- Add 1\/2 cup of the reserved broth to the onions and simmer for 2-3 minutes.\n\n5. Assemble and Serve:\n- Arrange the cooked noodles on a large serving platter.\n- Top with the boiled meat, either shredded or cut into large chunks.\n- Spoon the onion sauce over the meat and noodles.\n- Garnish with fresh parsley or dill, if desired.\n- Serve with the remaining hot broth in bowls on the side.\n\n\nEnjoy this hearty and comforting dish, perfect for sharing with family and friends! 🥩🍜",
      "unlockDate" : 759625200,
      "ingredients" : "For the Meat and Broth:\n\t•\t1-1.5 kg lamb, beef, or horse meat (with bones for flavor)\n\t•\t1 onion, peeled and halved\n\t•\t2 bay leaves\n\t•\t1 teaspoon black peppercorns\n\t•\tSalt (to taste)\n\t•\tWater (enough to cover the meat)\n\nFor the Noodles:\n\t•\t2 cups all-purpose flour\n\t•\t1 large egg\n\t•\t1\/2 teaspoon salt\n\t•\t1\/2 cup water (as needed to form a dough)\n\nFor the Onion Sauce:\n\t•\t2 large onions, thinly sliced\n\t•\t2 tablespoons butter or lamb fat\n\t•\t1\/2 cup of the reserved meat broth\n\nTo Serve:\n\t•\tFresh parsley or dill (optional, for garnish)",
