      "name" : "Ramen",
      "hasBeenOpened" : false,
      "id" : "FEFF9C3C-458C-42FB-ADCA-5CCFDB831765",
      "ingredients" : "For the Broth:\n\t•\t2 liters chicken or pork stock (or vegetable stock for vegetarian ramen)\n\t•\t4 cloves garlic, minced\n\t•\t1 tablespoon ginger, minced\n\t•\t2 tablespoons soy sauce\n\t•\t1 tablespoon miso paste (optional, for added depth)\n\t•\t1 tablespoon sesame oil\n\t•\t1 tablespoon mirin (sweet rice wine, optional)\n\t•\t1 teaspoon chili oil or togarashi (optional, for spice)\n\t•\tSalt, to taste\n\nFor the Noodles:\n\t•\t300 g fresh or dried ramen noodles (or any thin wheat noodles)\n\nToppings (Customize as Desired):\n\t•\t2 soft-boiled eggs (Ajitsuke Tamago, see instructions below)\n\t•\t100 g sliced cooked pork belly, chicken, or tofu\n\t•\t1 sheet nori (seaweed), cut into strips\n\t•\t1 cup bok choy or spinach, blanched\n\t•\t1\/2 cup corn kernels\n\t•\t2 green onions, sliced\n\t•\t1 tablespoon sesame seeds\n\t•\tChili oil, to taste\n",
      "unlockDate" : 759538800,
      "steps" : "1. Prepare the Broth:\n- In a large pot, heat sesame oil over medium heat. Add garlic and ginger and sauté until fragrant, about 1 minute.\n- Add the chicken or pork stock, soy sauce, miso paste, and mirin. Stir to combine and bring to a gentle simmer.\n- Let the broth simmer for 20-30 minutes to allow the flavors to meld. Adjust seasoning with salt and additional soy sauce as needed.\n\n2. Prepare the Noodles:\n- Cook the ramen noodles according to the package instructions. Drain and set aside.\n\n3. Prepare the Soft-Boiled Eggs (Ajitsuke Tamago):\n- Bring a pot of water to a boil. Carefully lower the eggs into the water and boil for 6-7 minutes for a slightly runny yolk.\n- Transfer the eggs to an ice bath to stop the cooking. Peel the eggs and set aside.\n\n4. Assemble the Ramen:\n- Divide the cooked noodles among serving bowls.\n- Ladle the hot broth over the noodles.\n- Top with sliced pork, tofu, or chicken, blanched greens, soft-boiled eggs (halved), corn, nori, green onions, and sesame seeds.\n- Drizzle with chili oil if desired.\n\n5. Serve:\n- Serve immediately and enjoy your warm, flavorful bowl of ramen!\n\n\nEnjoy your delicious homemade ramen! 🍜✨"
    },
    {
      "name" : "Pho (Vietnamese Noodle Soup)",
      "steps" : "1. Prepare the Broth:\n- Parboil the Bones: Place beef bones in a large pot, cover with water, and bring to a boil. Boil for 5 minutes, then drain and rinse the bones under cold water to remove impurities.\n- Char Aromatics: Char the onion and ginger over an open flame or in a hot, dry skillet until slightly blackened. This enhances the flavor.\n- Toast Spices: In a dry skillet, toast cinnamon sticks, star anise, cloves, coriander seeds, and fennel seeds for 1-2 minutes until fragrant.\n- Simmer the Broth: In a large stockpot, add the cleaned bones, optional brisket, charred onion and ginger, toasted spices, fish sauce, salt, sugar, and water. Bring to a boil, then reduce heat and simmer for 4-6 hours (or longer for deeper flavor). Skim off any foam or fat that rises to the surface.\n- Strain the Broth: Remove the bones, brisket (if using), onion, ginger, and spices. Strain the broth through a fine sieve and adjust seasoning with additional fish sauce, salt, or sugar.\n\n2. Prepare the Noodles:\n- Cook the rice noodles according to the package instructions. Drain and set aside.\n\n3. Prepare the Beef:\n- Thinly slice the raw beef against the grain. This is easiest if the beef is slightly frozen.\n- If using the optional brisket, slice it thinly after simmering.\n\n4. Assemble the Pho:\n- Divide the cooked noodles among serving bowls.\n- Place the raw sliced beef on top of the noodles (it will cook in the hot broth).\n- Ladle the hot broth over the noodles and beef, ensuring the beef is submerged to cook.\n\n5. Add Toppings and Serve:\n- Top with fresh bean sprouts, Thai basil, cilantro, green onions, and chili slices.\n- Serve with lime wedges, hoisin sauce, and Sriracha on the side.\n\nEnjoy your comforting and aromatic bowl of Pho! 🍜✨",
      "unlockDate" : 759798000,
      "ingredients" : "For the Broth:\n\t•\t1.5 kg beef bones (marrow or knuckle bones)\n\t•\t500 g beef brisket or chuck (optional, for serving)\n\t•\t1 large onion, halved\n\t•\t1 piece ginger (10 cm), sliced in half lengthwise\n\t•\t2 cinnamon sticks\n\t•\t4 star anise pods\n\t•\t4 cloves\n\t•\t1 tablespoon coriander seeds\n\t•\t1 tablespoon fennel seeds\n\t•\t1 tablespoon fish sauce\n\t•\t1 teaspoon salt\n\t•\t1-2 tablespoons rock sugar or granulated sugar\n\t•\t3 liters water\n\nFor the Noodles:\n\t•\t400 g dried or fresh rice noodles (Pho noodles)\n\nFor the Toppings:\n\t•\t300 g beef (sirloin, flank steak, or eye of round), thinly sliced\n\t•\tFresh bean sprouts\n\t•\tFresh Thai basil\n\t•\tFresh cilantro\n\t•\tGreen onions, sliced\n\t•\tLime wedges\n\t•\tFresh chili slices\n\t•\tHoisin sauce and Sriracha (optional, for serving)\n",
